        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italian_Village"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 1888‑built Berry Brothers Bolt Works still stands, a proud reminder of Italian Village’s industrial past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italian_Village"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "John the Baptist Italian Catholic Church, founded in 1896, was largely funded by immigrant businessman John Marzetti.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italian_Village"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Italian Village, a designated historic district, showcases Italianate and Queen Anne homes that line its narrow brick streets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
